     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,600 mg/day of ibuprofen is well into the toxic range, and I know of no indication that supports it. Past about 3,200 mg/day, analgesic and anti-inflammatory effect doesn't increase, but the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events does. The risk is high even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nIf the order was meant to be something else, I can enter it right away. For example:\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you believe this dose is warranted for a specific reason, please take it to clinical pharmacy or your hospital's high-risk order override process. They can review it and enter it through the appropriate channel."
